diff --git a/doc/api.rst b/doc/api.rst
index 2d65d5b3..7dea73f0 100644
--- a/doc/api.rst
+++ b/doc/api.rst
@@ -447,6 +447,12 @@ The library also supports convenient formatting of ranges and tuples::
   fmt::print("{}", t);
 
 
+Character ranges are formatted as lists of quoted, escaped characters, including
+when nested inside other ranges. String elements are quoted and escaped as well.
+This also applies to C++20 views such as ``std::views::split`` and ranges returned
+by value from ``std::views::transform``. Use an element format specifier to
+override the default debug formatting.
+
 NOTE: currently, the overload of ``fmt::join`` for iterables exists in the main
 ``format.h`` header, but expect this to change in the future.
 
